{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-124236" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ \\sqrt{v}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+1 \\\\ {v}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}3u-2 \\\\ 8-v\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124236" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\sqrt{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-2 \\\\ 8-v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u \\\\ -v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{3}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124236" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f878c5d873ff6311da3dc9245bc02e778b68b66ad92843dae863dbce586c6dbd"} {"question" "q-124236" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124236" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{3}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124236" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{3}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-{v}^{2} \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic terms ${u}^{2}$ and ${v}^{2}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}6v-4u \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4u+6v \\\\ 3u+3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{2}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v+9 \\\\ v-9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124251" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f878c5d873ff6311da3dc9245bc02e778b68b66ad92843dae863dbce586c6dbd"} {"question" "q-124251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1},$ ${T}_{2},$ and ${T}_{3}$"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124251" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ 1-{v}^{3}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u(v-1) \\\\ u-1\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9u+v \\\\ 2u+8v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}9 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the cubic term ${v}^{3}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the cross term $uv.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f878c5d873ff6311da3dc9245bc02e778b68b66ad92843dae863dbce586c6dbd"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{3}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124247" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{1}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u-1 \\\\ {e}^{v}\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v)\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is not affine since it contains the exponential term ${e}^{v}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{2}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v+2 \\\\ u-2v+4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8u+2v \\\\ u-2v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}8 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is not affine since it contains the term $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(u+v).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{2}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f878c5d873ff6311da3dc9245bc02e778b68b66ad92843dae863dbce586c6dbd"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{3}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124253" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{2}$ only"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n- ${T}_{1}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{2}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2} \\\\ -v\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${T}_{3}:[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}u+2 \\\\ u-v+1\\end{aligned}]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{1}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{1}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation ${T}_{1}$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{2}$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term ${u}^{2}.$\n\n- Transformation ${T}_{3}$ is affine. Notice that ${T}_{3}$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+2 \\\\ u-v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ u-v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124007" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f878c5d873ff6311da3dc9245bc02e778b68b66ad92843dae863dbce586c6dbd"} {"question" "q-124007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{1}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{2}$ only"] ["text" "${T}_{3}$ only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124007" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${T}_{1}$ and ${T}_{3}$ only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=4u+av-2,\\,y=bu+cv-3\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-v \\\\ 9u+5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u-v-2 \\\\ 9u+5v-3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=4u+(-1)v-2,\\,y=9u+5v-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-1+9+5=13.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124263" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f878c5d873ff6311da3dc9245bc02e778b68b66ad92843dae863dbce586c6dbd"} {"question" "q-124263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "13"] ["math" "14"] ["math" "15"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "8"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124263" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "13"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124261" "field" nil "attribute" "question/p