ed}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ -9u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+3 \\\\ -9u+4v+4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=1u+0v+3,\\,y=-9u+4v+4\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+0+4=5.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/state.json" "file_sha256" "62bcde169b15c900dd6d8c4d56c3d84fdc3434e265d02f17c24c76447e0afce0"} {"question" "q-124259" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f878c5d873ff6311da3dc9245bc02e778b68b66ad92843dae863dbce586c6dbd"} {"question" "q-124259" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-wo