ere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_1$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_1$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ v-2u+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u+v \\\\ -2u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_2$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ v-u\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-v \\\\ -u+v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn fact, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_3$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term $v^2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\\mathbf{T}_2$ only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9505.json" "file_sha256" "a86f53ae940196ebcb6a9d659d66c981838147b2d7c8d240d6eee16099a28771"} {"question" "e-9508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9508.json" "file_sha256" "e0667a9efd2b05d09a4f2e32b32e1102fb78daf5f51fc9bf04bb7a55b7e42a83"} {"question" "e-9508" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}]}}\\cdot \\overset{u}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}}+\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3u-v+1 \\\\ u-5v\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = 3u - v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{1}, \\qquad y = u + (\\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{-5})v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{0} \\, .\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+(-5)+0 = -4.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9508.json" "file_sha256" "e0667a9efd2b05d09a4f2e32b32e1102fb78daf5f51fc9bf04bb7a55b7e42a83"} {"question" "e-9506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9506.json" "file_sha256" "063600f9abe5c5578be06f245958b40419fee0fc3a7f0ebf1b3953a6bf833f4f"} {"question" "e-9506" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u,$ and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2,$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v-6 \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5u+v \\\\ 2u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033859/example-9506.json" "file_sha256" "063600f9abe5c5578be06f245958b40419fee0fc3a7f0ebf1b3953a6bf833f4f"}] "usage" {"e-9505" [] "e-9508" [] "e-9506" [] "q-124271" [] "q-124088" [] "q-124007" []} "basis" 1242 "retractions" [[17592186172225 :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n1. $T_{1}: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u + v \\\\ v - u\\end{bmatrix}$\n2. $T_{2}: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u^{2} \\\\ -v\\end{bmatrix}$\n3. $T_{3}: \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}⟶\\begin{bmatrix}u + 2 \\\\ u - v + 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186172229 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$x = au + 4v, y =-5u + bv + c$\nis shown below. What is the value of $a + b + c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186172226 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$x = u - 2v + 1, y = u + v - 2$\nis shown below. What is the value of $a + b + c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186171830 :question/problem "Which of the following are affine transformations?\n\n1. $\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}$\n2. $\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}$\n3. $\\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186171830 :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u$, and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2$, and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWith this in mind, let's look at each transformation in turn.\n\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_1$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_1$ can be expressed as\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}|= \\begin{bmatrix}u + v \\\\ v - 2u + 1\\end{bmatrix}; = \\begin{bmatrix}u + v \\\\ -2u + v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}; = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(A) \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(u) + \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(b)$.\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is affine. Notice that $\\mathbf{T}_2$ can be expressed as\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}|= \\begin{bmatrix}u - v \\\\ v - u\\end{bmatrix}; = \\begin{bmatrix}u - v \\\\ -u + v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}; = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(A) \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(u) + \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(b)$.\nIn fact, the transformation $\\mathbf{T}_2$ is a linear transformation.\n- Transformation $\\mathbf{T}_3$ is not affine since it contains the quadratic term $v^2$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$\\mathbf{T}_1$ and $\\mathbf{T}_2$ only.\""] [17592186171832 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n$x = 3u-v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{a}, \\qquad y = u + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{b}v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{c}$\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186171832 :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u$, and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2$, and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nWe can carry out the matrix operations using the matrix form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(A) \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(u) + \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}^(⏞)^(b) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}3u - v \\\\ u - 5v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}3u - v + 1 \\\\ u - 5v\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding elements, we obtain\n\n$$\nx = 3u - v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{1}, \\qquad y = u + (\\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{-5})v + \\bbox[Gainsboro,2pt]{0} \\,\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+(-5)+0 = -4\n$$"] [17592186171831 :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n$x = 5u + v - 6, \\qquad y = 2u + 4v$\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c$?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186171831 :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $\\mathbf T:\\mathbb R^2\\rightarrow\\mathbb R^2$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf x = A \\mathbf u + \\mathbf b\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf x, \\mathbf u$, and $\\mathbf b$ are column vectors in $\\mathbb R^2$, and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n$\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}5u + v - 6 \\\\ 2u + 4v\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}5u + v \\\\ 2u + 4v\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(A) \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}u \\\\ v\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(u) + \\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(b)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c = 1+2+0 = 3\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186168554 17592186168555 17592186168556 17592186168557 17592186168558 17592186168560 17592186168561 17592186168562 17592186168563 17592186168564 17592186168578 17592186168579 17592186168580 17592186168581 17592186168582] "immutable_fields" [[17592186168553 :answer-field/correct] [17592186168553 :answer-field/id] [17592186168553 :answer-field/key] [17592186168553 :answer-field/type] [17592186168559 :answer-field/correct] [17592186168559 :answer-field/id] [17592186168559 :answer-field/key] [17592186168559 :answer-field/type] [17592186168577 :answer-field/correct] [17592186168577 :answer-field/id] [17592186168577 :answer-field/key] [17592186168577 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
